You have the option to do exactly that. Hearse has
command line options for deleting the existing bones
file and returning a bones file for some random
level, or for replacing the existing bones file with
one for the same level. Hearse's other mode is to
keep the existing bones file, and download some
other random bones level in exchange for the one
uploaded, but that mode doesn't, yet, have a command
line flag.

Hearse comes set up by default in "replace" mode.
Since "keep" mode doesn't have an override, I
changed my setup to default to "keep" mode,

  Extract from Hearse.ini:

    # Determines how Hearse behaves.
    # Keep = Leaves your bones after upload, downloads
    # ones of a random level
    # Delete = Deletes your bones after upload,
    # downloads ones of a random level
    # Replace = Deletes your bones after upload,
    # downloads ones of the same level

    # The default behaviour is 'replace'

    Mode = keep

then added two (MS-Windows) batch files, one to
override to "delete" mode, one to override to
"replace" mode.

  HearseLose.bat:

    @echo off
    .\hearse /d

  HearseReplace.bat:

    @echo off
    .\hearse /m


