One of the reasons my games don't last long is that
I _love_ bones files, and so keep lots of them
around, 73 different bones files right now, but only
for 32 of the levels, the most for any one level
being eight for both DLVL4 and DLVL5. Mostly, that
habit is way fatal to my PCs, but a nasty, nasty
bones file is a great puzzle to solve, I keep backup
bones file copies and work at the same ones over and
over until I "solve" them, frying lots of PCs to
solve each one, so my lack of ascensions is likely
to last "forever".

Oh, well. It's my PC, and it's fun for me.

Since I rarely get very far down in the dungeon, or
see artifacts, these are hardly "packed bones", but
they do tend to accumulate "stuff", which isn't much
use, since it's been years since I've polypiled. Of
course, when I carry away the good stuff and then
manage to come back to die in some incredible YASD,
the goodies and ghosts and lethal monsters get
weeded out almost as often as enriched in the new
version of the bones file. I just lost a PC with
24,000 zorkmids in a chest on another level (no BoH
yet, so no way to carry that much weight).

Once I get a full kit of a mix of my PC's bones
files and ones Hearsed in, I'll change to using
Hearse's Replace mode, and eventually almost none of
the ones I see when playing will be "mine".

